{{also|Brose}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From the [[Doric]] dialect of North East Scotland, from earlier [[browes]], from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|broez}}, nominative of {{m|fro|broet||stew, soup made from meat broth}} (French {{m|fr|brouet}}) diminutive of {{m|fro|breu}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|brodium}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*bruþą||broth}}. See [[broth]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|Scotland}} [[oatmeal|Oatmeal]] mixed with [[boiling]] [[water]].

====Derived terms====
* [[brosy]], [[brosey]]
* [[brosy-faced]]

